15. Overseer Fights

The prototype should include a few boss-style rule changes.

These should be limited in number but clearly distinct.

Example Overseers
The Taxer

All gold gain is halved this encounter

The Shroud

Spades mastery effects are disabled this encounter

The Split Crown

Hands with only one suit lose 20% final score

This last one is especially good because it reinforces your anti-Flush design philosophy.

16. Anti-Flush Bias Design

This is an important balancing principle.

Since suits are important, the design must avoid making Flush the obvious dominant strategy.

Core Anti-Flush Rules
Suit XP is gained per hand presence, not per suit card count
Suit effects are role-based, not mostly linear-per-card bonuses
Some suit effects reward mixed presence better than all-one-suit stacking
Bosses and Champions can reward diversity
Diamonds specifically should not reward 4–5 of the same suit excessively

This keeps:

Flush viable
but not mandatory
